T12:00\" data-lat=\"35.1010\" data-lng=\"129.0280\">\n  <div class=\"event-time\">12:00</div>\n  <div class=\"event-body\">\n    <div class=\"event-tags\"><span class=\"tag meal\">🎬 Lunch</span></div>\n    <div class=\"event-name\">BIFF Square — Street Food</div>\n    <div class=\"event-notes\">Busan International Film Festival's home street is lined with film star handprints and great street food stalls. Try:\n      <ul>\n        <li>씨앗 호떡 (Ssiat Hotteok) — Busan's signature seed-filled hotteok, crispy and caramelised</li>\n        <li>Soondae (blood sausage) with tteok</li>\n        <li>Eomuk (fish cake) skewers with broth</li>\n      </ul>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"event-links\">\n      <a href=\"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=BIFF+Square+Nampo+Busan\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"maps-link\">📍 BIFF Square</a>\n      <a href=\"https://map.naver.com/p/search/BIFF광장+부산\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"maps-link naver-link\">🗺 Naver</a>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n```\n\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"section-header\">Afternoon — Jagalchi & Songdo</div>\n\n<div class=\"event-card afternoon\" data-dt=\"2026-08-06T14:00\" data-lat=\"35.0968\" data-lng=\"129.0301\">\n  <div class=\"event-time\">14:00</div>\n  <div class=\"event-body\">\n    <div class=\"event-tags\"><span class=\"tag activity\">🦀 Market</span></div>\n    <div class=\"event-name\">Jagalchi Fish Market</div>\n    <div class=\"event-notes\">Korea's largest seafood market — a Busan institution. Rows of live sea creatures: abalone, sea cucumber, flounder, crab, and more. The market women (자갈치아지매) are legendary. You can buy fish upstairs and have it prepared for you to eat on-site.\n      <ul>\n        <li>Go to the upper floors for sit-down fresh fish meals</li>\n        <li>Haggling is expected</li>\n        <li>Morning is busiest but afternoon still lively</li>\n      </ul>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"event-links\">\n      <a href=\"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Jagalchi+Market+Busan\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"maps-link\">📍 Jagalchi</a>\n      <a href=\"https://map.naver.com/p/search/자갈치시장\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"maps-link naver-link\">🗺 Naver</a>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"event-card afternoon\" data-dt=\"2026-08-06T16:00\" data-lat=\"35.0853\" data-lng=\"129.0131\">\n  <div class=\"event-time\">16:00</div>\n  <div class=\"event-body\">\n    <div class=\"event-tags\"><span class=\"tag activity\">🚡 Cable Car</span></div>\n    <div class=\"event-name\">Songdo Beach Cable Car</div>\n    <div class=\"event-notes\">Glass-bottomed gondolas above a dramatic rocky coastline — connects Songdo Beach to Amnam Park. 1.6km over the sea, ~10 min each way. Stunning views over the Busan coastline and islands.</div>\n    <div class=\"event-links\">\n      <a href=\"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Songdo+Beach+Cable+Car+Busan\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"maps-link\">📍 Songdo Cable Car</a>\n      <a href=\"https://map.naver.com/p/search/송도해상케이블카\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"maps-link naver-link\">🗺 Naver</a>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n```\n\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"section-header\">Sunset</div>\n\n<div class=\"event-card evening\" data-dt=\"2026-08-06T18:00\" data-lat=\"35.0817\" data-lng=\"129.1208\">\n  <div class=\"event-time\">18:00</div>\n  <div class=\"event-body\">\n    <div class=\"event-tags\"><span class=\"tag activity\">🌁 Viewpoint</span></div>\n    <div class=\"event-name\">Oryukdo Skywalk</div>\n    <div class=\"event-notes\">Glass-floored skywalk protruding over the rocky cliffs with Oryukdo (Five-Six Islands) in view — Korea's southernmost point before the open sea. Spectacular sunset spot. Free entry. Glass shoe covers provided.</div>\n    <div class=\"event-links\">\n      <a href=\"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Oryukdo+Skywalk+Busan\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"maps-link\">📍 Oryukdo Skywalk</a>\n      <a href=\"https://map.naver.com/p/search/오륙도스카이워크\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"maps-link naver-link\">🗺 Naver</a>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n```\n\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"section-header\">Dinner</div>\n\n<div class=\"event-card meal\" data-dt=\"2026-08-06T19:30\" data-lat=\"35.1590\" data-lng=\"129.1630\">\n  <div class=\"event-time\">19:30</div>\n  <div class=\"event-body\">\n    <div class=\"event-tags\"><span class=\"tag meal\">🦐 Feast</span></div>\n    <div class=\"event-name\">Seafood Feast — Last Busan Dinner</div>\n    <div class=\"event-notes\">Final Busan night — go big! Options:\n      <ul>\n        <li>Haeundae 회센터 (raw fish centre) — multiple restaurants, pick your fish live</li>\n        <li>Grilled lobster or snow crab</li>\n        <li>Haemul pajeon + makgeolli (seafood pancake with rice wine)</li>\n        <li>Ganjang gejang (if you missed it in Seoul)</li>\n      </ul>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"event-links\">\n      <a href=\"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=seafood+feast+restaurant+Busan\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"maps-link\">📍 Find Seafood</a>\n      <a href=\"https://map.naver.com/p/search/부산+해산물+맛집\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"maps-link naver-link\">🗺 Naver</a>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n```\n\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"note-box\"><strong>KTX tomorrow</strong> — buy tickets early. Target 10:00–11:00 AM departure from Busan station. Journey to Seoul ~2.5 hrs. Book at Korail website or at the station.</div>\n```\n"},"formats":{"html":{"identifier":{"display-name":"HTML","target-format":"html","base-format":"html"},"execute":{"fig-width":7,"fig-height":5,"fig-format":"retina","fig-dpi":96,"df-print":"default","error":false,"eval":true,"cache":null,"freeze":false,"echo":true,"output":true,"warning":true,"include":true,"keep-md":false,"keep-ipynb":false,"ipynb":null,"enabled":null,"daemon":null,"daemon-restart":false,"debug":false,"ipynb-filters":[],"ipynb-shell-interactivity":null,"plotly-connected":true,"engine":"markdown"},"render":{"keep-tex":false,"keep-typ":false,"keep-source":false,"keep-hidd